<header><p class="st-kicker">other · Poland, Lithuania and Russia</p><h1 class="st-title">Free Territory</h1><p class="st-meta">1918 CE – 1921 CE · capital Huliaipole</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">Nestor Makhno's anarchist zone in south-eastern Ukraine, run by peasant councils and defended by a revolutionary army in the Civil War.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nestor-makhno">Nestor Makhno</a>, an anarchist from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/huliaipole">Huliaipole</a>, organised peasant partisans against the Austro-German occupiers and the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/ukrainian-state">Ukrainian State</a> in 1918. As the Revolutionary Insurgent Army of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ukraine">Ukraine</a> grew, it controlled a large area between the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dnieper">Dnieper</a> and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sea-of-azov">Sea of Azov</a>, which anarchists called the Free Territory.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>The movement rejected any state, organising regional congresses of peasants, workers and insurgents, free soviets and communes, while anarchist thinkers such as <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/voline">Volin</a> ran its cultural work. In practice it was a military zone held by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nestor-makhno">Makhno</a>'s highly mobile cavalry and machine-gun carts. The insurgents fought Germans, nationalists and Bolsheviks, and in September 1919 their victory at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-peregonovka">Peregonovka</a> disrupted <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/anton-denikin">Denikin</a>'s march on <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/moscow">Moscow</a>.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>In 1920 <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nestor-makhno">Makhno</a> allied with the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/red-army">Red Army</a> against <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pyotr-wrangel">Wrangel</a>, but once the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/white-movement">Whites</a> were beaten the Bolsheviks turned on the insurgents in November. After months of fighting Makhno escaped to <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/kingdom-of-romania">Romania</a> in August 1921 and died in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/paris">Paris</a> in 1934.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><div class="st-emblem" role="img" aria-label="other, 1918 CE – 1921 CE"><svg viewBox="0 0 100 100" aria-hidden="true"><ellipse cx="44" cy="56" rx="16" ry="24"/><path d="M44 34 V78"/><path d="M68 20 V84"/><path d="M68 20 L63 30 H73 Z"/></svg><p class="st-emblem-type">other</p><p class="st-emblem-region">Poland, Lithuania and Russia</p><div class="st-span" aria-hidden="true"><span class="st-span-bar" style="left:97.87%;width:1.20%"></span></div><div class="st-span-axis" aria-hidden="true"><span>3000 BCE</span><span>1 CE</span><span>2000</span></div></div><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1918 CE – 1921 CE</dd><dt>Century</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>other</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>tribal</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Huliaipole</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Nestor Makhno, Volin</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Ukrainian, Russian</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/ukraine">Ukraine</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Makhnovshchina, Makhnovia</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1920&amp;focus=free-territory" aria-label="Free Territory on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="5526 507 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Free Territory lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M5846 763L5820 533"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M5820 533h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M5846 763h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M5846 763h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks Huliaipole. <a href="/atlas?year=1920&amp;focus=free-territory">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>

